---
title: Greek Turkey Meatballs With Tzatziki
servings: 2
cuisine: greek
main_protein: turkey
prep_time: "30 minutes"
cook_time: "10 minutes"
tags:
  - lunch
prep:
  - Mince 2 garlic cloves
  - Grate 0.25 large red onion
  - Chop 0.25 cup fresh dill
  - Make the Tzatziki Sauce
---

In a #large bowl{}, add @ground turkey{1%lb} (93/7 lean preferred) and @garlic{2%cloves}, minced.

Grate @red onion{0.25} (of a large onion) into turkey, alternatively chop red onion very small.

Add @egg{1}, @breadcrumbs{0.5%cup} (or almond flour), @fresh dill{0.25%cup}, chopped, @dried oregano{0.5%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp}, and @black pepper{0.5%tsp}. Mix until just combined, I use my hands.

Form into 14 meatballs.

Heat #saucepan{} with @olive oil{2%tbsp} over medium heat. Once hot, add meatballs and cook for ~{7%minutes}, turning constantly to ensure even cooking on all sides. Once meatballs reach 165F they are done.

While meatballs are cooking, make Tzatziki Sauce.

Serve over rice!

-- Tzatziki: use the separate Tzatziki Sauce recipe (tzatziki-sauce.cook).
